-- title:
--   Lifting a Frobenius-fixed regular function on the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a nonzero level $N$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$; fix modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (X^q - Y)(X - Y^q) \bmod q$, and integrality hypotheses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ asserting that the Hecke maps `heckeAlphaBar` and `heckeBetaBar` at level $N$ and prime $q$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ have integral underlying ring homomorphisms. Let $P$ be a place specialisation for these data: in particular it provides a map `P.sp` from places of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(X_0(N))$-type field $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,N$ to places of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N = k(j(q), j(q^N))$, together with its compatibility clauses. Assume $q \nmid N$ and let $\bar g$ lie in $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ and satisfy: every Laurent coefficient $c_n$ of $\bar g$ obeys $c_n^q = c_n$, and $\bar g$ lies in the valuation subring of every place $u$ of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ over $k$ which is affine geometric, i.e. for which both $j(q)$ and $j(q^N)$ lie in that valuation subring. Then there are a Laurent series $g_0$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, a Laurent series $y$ over $A$, and an element $g$ of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,N$ such that $g_0$ belongs to $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,N$ (the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions at level $N$), $g$ is the coefficientwise image of $g_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, $y$ has the same coefficientwise image (so $g_0$ has $A$-integral coefficients), the expansion of $\bar g$ is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $red$, and $g$ lies in the valuation subring of every place $U$ of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,N$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose specialisation $P.sp\,U$ is affine geometric.
--
--   This is the lifting step for the Igusa/Deligne–Rapoport good-reduction picture of the affine modular curve of level $N$ away from $q$: a function on the special fibre with coefficients in $\mathbb{F}_q$ and no poles on the affine part is lifted, through the $q$-expansion, to a modular function of level $N$ with $A$-integral expansion reducing to it and regular at all characteristic-zero places specialising into the affine part. It is used in the analysis of supersingular places, in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_ord_sub_pow_sq_eq_one_of_mem_ssPlaces`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_ord_sub_pow_sq_eq_one_of_mem_ssPlaces).
